{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430145-what-s-up-with-werewolves-detecting-one-another","id":430145,"title":"What's up with Werewolves detecting one another?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T06:11:13-08:00","id":430145,"title":"What's up with Werewolves detecting one another?","content":"Page 61 of Werewolf states, under Hishu,<br /> <br /> &quot;Most Uratha are most comfortable in human shape. Others see it as just another tool to use on the hunt. While wearing the Hishu skin, a werewolf hides amongst humanity. Efforts to pick her out of the crowd and identify her as somehow supernatural fail, even if those attempts are supernatural in their own right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 95 of Werewolf states, under Senses --&gt; Smell<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolves can also identify each other and Wolf-Blooded by smell. Doing so requires a Wits + Primal Urge roll, though this takes an instant action and she has to get in close to the character to be sure. Whether she uses the close press of a nightclub crowd or a tight-knit mob at a riot, she has to invade her suspect\u2019s personal space&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 96 of Werewolf states, under Hishu,<br /> <br /> It's actually what it doesn't state. Despite this being where forms are mechanically defined we don't get a repeat of Hishu's detection immunity. It should really be here if it's a thing.<br /> '<br /> Page 98 of Werewolf states, under Hunter Aspect<br /> <br /> &quot;Uratha know each other at a glance. Apex predators smell their own. This crosses all three of the Uratha\u2019s sensory fields; every single sense can identify one Uratha to another, as the man, the wolf, and the spirit all carry a prominent, forceful aura.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 92 of Blood and Smoke states, in the sidebar &quot;Others and the Predatory Aura&quot; state<br /> <br /> &quot;Other denizens of the World of Darkness may have similar auras. Most well-known is the feral mien of the werewolves. When Kindred notice werewolves, they feel physiological responses they<br /> never otherwise experience, such as goose pimples along their arms, and chills down their backs. They feel the adrenaline surge in the pit of the stomach that humans associate with danger and tense excitement.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think some of these entries are in error? I'm not sure how to parse this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:36:46-08:00","id":430332,"title":"","content":"In regards to pg 98, I think it answers your question: It's in regards to the Hunter's Aspect. If I'm interpreting it properly I believe that applies when the pack or that wolf in particular is under the Siskur-Dah. It's only at that time that the Hunter's Aspect comes forward and that's when it becomes easy for the wolves to notice eachother. I'm thinking that the Siskur-Dah causes an immense predatory aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:48:38-08:00","id":430342,"title":"","content":"The word Siskur-Dah isn't written anywhere on that page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:57:39-08:00","id":430356,"title":"","content":"The detection immunity is listed under 'Sheep's Clothing.'<br /> <br /> As for the rest, it seems like you automatically detect Uratha unless they're concealing it, where you might have to smell them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T18:56:14-08:00","id":430961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430145-what-s-up-with-werewolves-detecting-one-another?p=430356#post430356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The detection immunity is listed under 'Sheep's Clothing.'<br /> <br /> As for the rest, it seems like you automatically detect Uratha unless they're concealing it, where you might have to smell them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing; Sheep's clothing is a small penalty to detect them in a crowd or trail them. That's very much not a prevention to supernatural detection like is implied earlier in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to the original post, I completely agree that the Hunter's Aspect page seems to contradict the Wolf Senses page, which gives mechanics that just don't fit what the HA page says. I also dislike that the Hunter's Aspect page doesn't actually talk about things like predatory aura, as opposed to blood and smoke which does, and if they can sense a Vampire similarly (Yes, blah blah blah they might be able to hear lack of a heartbeat if they focus, but that's a completely different thing).<br /> <br /> Really, overall, as much as I love Werewolf 2 overall, the Hunter's Aspect page seems like whoever wrote it not only didn't look at any other lines, but they didn't talk with any other developer working on the same dang book. It just seems like that page was thrown in last minute, without checking anything over and without actually considering what needs to be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T17:35:12-07:00","id":445104,"title":"","content":"Going by each point as a number, this is the best I can figure it all out. It is confusing.<br /> <br /> 1. This is not an automatic detection failure. It is an indication that the detection can fail, see Sheep's Clothing.<br /> 2. This is for Urhan and Urshul, not Hishu and Dalu, unless the werewolf chooses to use wolf senses.<br /> 3. Sheep's Clothing<br /> 4. This seems out of place, but I reconcile it by saying they would be using wolf senses and it is not automatic, see Wolf's Senses.<br /> 5. Kindred can detect a werewolf if they can beat Sheep's Clothing and would be able to tell the strange human is a werewolf if they know about them.<br /> <br /> Basically, werewolves are difficult to detect when in human form, but this is less effective when under specific scrutiny. You might not detect anything if you walk onto a crowded train, but if you &quot;sniff&quot; each of the other passengers then you could find your wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T01:11:48-07:00","id":451366,"title":"","content":"For the crossover part with blood &amp; smoke I also made a question there where a discussion sprang from:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other\"> 2.0. Beasts recognizing each other - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444603-2-0-beasts-recognizing-each-other </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In the new vampire core rules it was mentioned as a sidenote that they feel that werwwolves have some sort of beast inside of them (thus they feel at unease near them). But it was never implied further there. In the new core for werewolf I didn't see any mentioning there at all about their wolfish side in </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It really seems that there were different people involved each in writing the hunter aspect / sheep clothing / predatory aura rules as they seem inconsistent to each other in wording. OR are left deliberately open formulated (so either an internal communicatoins stumble or it was left a bit open/contradictionary on purpose so the STs can decide (although if that is the intention then the different possibilities of how to interpret things would have been nicer in a side box.......in their current incarnation they just confuse sadly))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}